From 47e78cb69431de08cfa525415154d1b12fba271f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: b1air <dimazzzzz342@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:57:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Add overview: every workspace of an output side by side,
 live

`overview toggle|show|hide` shows every workspace of the focused output
in a grid, each its own tiling tree drawn scaled down (scenefx's
wlr_scene_tree_set_scale), so windows keep drawing at their own size.
The active workspace shrinks from the full screen into its place as the
others come in on dark cards; leaving reverses it. A click on a
workspace, or Enter on the one picked with the arrows, goes there;
Escape, or a click beside them, leaves.

`overview_swipe <fingers>` brings it in with a swipe up and takes it away
with a swipe down, following the fingers; letting go finishes it, or puts
it back when the fingers did not go far or fast enough. Sideways swipes
with those fingers still go to the gesture bindings.

Floating windows sit in one layer for all workspaces and are hidden
while it is up; the special workspace is not shown. Workspaces still
sliding or held by a swipe are put in place first, and a switch made
from the overview does not slide.

Needs scenefx with wlr_scene_tree_set_scale (src/scenefx patch 0002).
